    "updated_at": "2025-10-05T07:24:54Z",
    "body": "Curious what @whatwg/a11y makes of this, but introducing alternative APIs is not free. It ends up breaking websites for people with older user agents. It's likely it will be introduced with its own set of mistakes, etc. (And somewhat besides the point, but \"unclickable\" would be rather mouse-centric and might not at all convey the state correctly to readers of the code.)\n\nI think it's relatively common to talk about a \"thing\" being disabled, such as an alarm, but maybe I'm missing something.",
