    "created_at": "2025-10-06T12:22:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-06T12:22:35Z",
    "body": "Entire models have been developed to [conceptualize disability](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Models_of_disability), and every one of them has its supporters and detractors because it is, ultimately, subjective.\n\nSpeaking for myself, I'm comfortable with the name of the `disabled` attribute because it has little/no correlation with how I think of myself as a person with a disability, but I don't think this is the time or place for these discussions.\n\nI will note though that the use of \"unclickable\" to characterise an element with the `disabled` attribute might itself be considered ablist, since disabled elements are unusable by everyone not just mouse users. Given the topic, this is a curious choice of language to use.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
