    "created_at": "2025-10-08T15:14:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-08T15:57:44Z",
    "body": "well i appreciate that y'all chatted about it! \n\nto @LJWatson's point, yes, people's experiences with words are subjective. \n\n i have a degree in the study of marginalized communities and historical-critical analysis of text from an excellent university (it took me awhile to figure out i wanted to do SE) BUT my take on what's happening here is just a hunch based on all that - it's not like i looked for records of the discussion that actually caused them to choose the word 'disabled' here. \n\nAnd anyway my guess is at least one (and probably multiple) of the people who responded was responding as an authority on behalf of @whatwg/a11y and also definitely at least one other member of the disabled community so even if i disagree with it i can definitely respect it as a very fair ruling. \n\nyes yes, there are different ways of using a button. unactionable might be a better word then. \n\nanyway, thanks yall!",
